From: BC-250 maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] drm/amdgpu: advertise a stable VKMS EDID

Attach the EDID property omitted by virtual connectors, then publish a
synthetic BC250 identity and derive the connector modes from its EDID. Keep
the existing 60 Hz modes except two CVT modes beyond the EDID clock limit;
prefer 1920x1080.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_vkms.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_vkms.c
@@ -91,49 +91,48 @@
 	.atomic_destroy_state = drm_atomic_helper_connector_destroy_state,
 };
 
+/*
+ * Advertised 60 Hz modes: 640x480, 720x480, 800x600, 848x480, 1024x768,
+ * 1152x768, 1280x720, 1280x800, 1280x854, 1280x960, 1280x1024,
+ * 1400x1050, 1440x900, 1600x1200, 1680x1050, 1920x1080, 1920x1200,
+ * 2560x1440, 2560x1600, 3840x2160, and 4096x2160. The legacy 4096x3112
+ * and 3656x2664 CVT modes exceed EDID's 16-bit 10 kHz pixel-clock field.
+ */
+static const u8 amdgpu_vkms_edid[] = {
